      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 11 & -8 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -49 & 36 \\\\ 2 & 11 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 56 & -49\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below $a_{21}=2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 11 & -8 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}-4R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -49 & 36 \\\\ 2 & 11 & -8 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{3}:=R_{3}+5R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -49 & 36 \\\\ 2 & 11 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 56 & -49\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}-4R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3}+5R_{2}$.",
