    "question": {
      ":question/id": "83563381-d19b-5dac-8661-5921b412c32c",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 11\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 42 & 17 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 14\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below $a_{21}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}+8R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 42 & 17 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{3}:=R_{3}+3R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 42 & 17 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 14\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}+8R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3}+3R_{2}$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
